    {
      "id": "p0170-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In the English script, Temmies often call themselves \"temmie\", \"TEMMIE\", or \"tEMMIE\" - capitalization seemingly has no meaning for them. In other instances, Temmies simply call themselves \"tem\". To replicate this unusual English wordplay, the translator devised a simple system:",
        "raw": "In the English script, Temmies often call themselves \"temmie\", \"TEMMIE\",\nor \"tEMMIE\" - capitalization seemingly has no meaning for them. In other\ninstances, Temmies simply call themselves \"tem\". To replicate this unusual\nEnglish wordplay, the translator devised a simple system:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29570555,
          0.31037143,
          0.88596215,
          0.37740714
