    {
      "id": "p0170-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Basically, both Japanese names for \"Temmie\" are pronounced the same, but the misspelled name mixes two Japanese writing systems in an unexpected way. The resulting misspelling, which combines the kanji character 手 (te, \"hand\") with the katakana characters ミー (mī), is bizarre, funny, and memorable.",
        "raw": "Basically, both Japanese names for \"Temmie\" are pronounced the same, but the\nmisspelled name mixes two Japanese writing systems in an unexpected way.\nThe resulting misspelling, which combines the kanji character =f: (te, \"hand\")\nwith the katakana characters 2 - (mf), is bizarre, funny, and memorable.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29570555,
          0.48330714,
          0.90541499,
          0.54935
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29138383,
          0.48259286,
          0.90745835,
          0.55042143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          21,
          22,
          23,
          24
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "两种日文名字读音相同，但错误写法出人意料地混合了两种文字：把汉字“手”（te，手）与片假名“ミー”（mī）拼在一起。这样的错字古怪、好笑，又让人记得住。",
        "status": "draft",
