    {
      "id": "p0170-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In English, Temmies sound like hyperactive, energetic girls. In Japanese, Temmies use a variety of unique speech patterns to sound equally hyperactive and energetic. And although they don't use pronouns very often, Temmies in the Japanese script use the youthful and feminine personal pronoun achishi.",
        "raw": "In English, Temmies sound like hyperactive, energetic girls. In Japanese,\nTemmies use a variety of unique speech patterns to sound equally hyperactive\nand energetic. And although they don't use pronouns very often, Temmies in\nthe Japanese script use the youthful and feminine personal pronoun achishi.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
