    {
      "id": "p0170-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In the English script, one unusual Temmie uses proper grammar and introduces himself as \"Bob\". For the Japanese script, the translator left Bob's name as-is, and gave him a polite, grammatically correct speech pattern. As part of this, Bob uses the boyish pronoun boku.",
